# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clear Skies Forecaster — optional environment configuration
# Copy to .env.local and adjust. EVERYTHING here is optional: the map works
# out of the box with the keyless chain below. NEVER commit real keys
# (.env.local is git-ignored; this example file must stay placeholder-only).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle at BUILD time —
# restart `npm run dev` or re-run `npm run build` after changing them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Preferred basemap provider (head of the fallback chain):
#   esri  — Esri World Dark Gray, keyless, dark theme (DEFAULT)
#   carto — CARTO Dark Matter; REQUIRES NEXT_PUBLIC_CARTO_API_KEY below,
#           otherwise the app warns and falls back to the keyless chain
#   osm   — OpenStreetMap standard tiles, keyless (light theme)
# At runtime each provider is verified (tile pixel probe + error monitoring);
# on failure the map steps ONCE to the next keyless fallback (esri → osm),
# never retrying endlessly.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_PROVIDER=esri

# Optional CARTO basemap API key.
# Since late August 2026 CARTO stamps every KEYLESS basemaps.cartocdn.com tile
# with an "API KEY REQUIRED" watermark, so keyless CARTO is no longer used.
# If you want the original CARTO Dark Matter look, request a free key
# (5M tile requests/month, no approval queue) at:
#   https://carto.com/basemaps/apikey
# and set it here in .env.local. Leave unset/empty to use the keyless default.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_CARTO_API_KEY=
